          {
            "title": "Intro",
            "id": 82512,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Gli elenchi ordinati sono utili quando vogliamo capire in che posizione si trovano i singoli punti dati, come i punteggi, rispetto agli altri.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"11\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"11\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"7\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /></content></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Method call",
            "id": 82513,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Per ordinare una lista come <code>scores</code>, scriviamo il nome della lista, un punto <code>.</code> e poi <code>sort()</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"scores.sort()\" /><text type=\"break\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"23\" endIndex=\"29\" /><option startIndex=\"29\" endIndex=\"30\" /><option startIndex=\"30\" endIndex=\"36\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>scores</code>, seguito da <code>.</code> e infine <code>sort()</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Display",
            "id": 82517,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>L'ordinamento modifica la lista, quindi quando riutilizziamo o visualizziamo la lista con <code>print(scores)</code>, apparirà ordinata.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"scores.sort()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(scores)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"37\" endIndex=\"50\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 3, 6, 12]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di digitare <code>print(scores)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Ascending order",
            "id": 82601,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Quando usi <code>sort()</code> su un elenco di numeri come <code>scores</code>, i numeri vengono ordinati in ordine crescente.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"scores.sort()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(scores)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"29\" endIndex=\"30\" /><option startIndex=\"30\" endIndex=\"34\" /><option startIndex=\"34\" endIndex=\"35\" /><option startIndex=\"35\" endIndex=\"36\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 3, 6, 12]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>.</code>, seguito da <code>sort</code> e poi <code>(</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Float and Integer",
            "id": 82514,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Le liste che contengono sia valori con virgola mobile come <code>9.99</code> sia numeri interi vengono ordinate in base ai loro valori numerici.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"prices = [\" /><text value=\"13\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"9.99\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"7.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"prices.sort()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(prices)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"14\" endIndex=\"18\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[7.5, 9.99, 10, 13]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di digitare <code>9.99</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Negative numbers",
            "id": 82515,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Quando usi <code>sort()</code> su un elenco di numeri positivi e negativi come <code>temperatures</code>, il numero più piccolo, <code>-3</code>, viene per primo.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"temperatures = [\" /><text value=\"-1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\",\" /><text value=\"-3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"temperatures.sort()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(temperatures)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"39\" endIndex=\"45\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[-3, -1, 2]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di digitare <code>sort()</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Sorting strings",
            "id": 82516,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Quando usi <code>sort()</code> su un elenco di stringhe come <code>names</code>, gli elementi vengono ordinati in ordine alfabetico.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"names = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Cloe&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Ana&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Bill&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"names.sort()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(names)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"32\" endIndex=\"37\" /><option startIndex=\"37\" endIndex=\"38\" /><option startIndex=\"38\" endIndex=\"42\" /><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"43\" /><option startIndex=\"43\" endIndex=\"44\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"['Ana', 'Bill', 'Cloe']\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>names</code>, seguito da <code>.</code> e poi <code>sort</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
